\f0\fs24 \cf0 Notes: \
\
The webusb tool, requires attaching each device, clicking on copy and pasting on another text editor. The better and more efficient way would be to automatically copy the read results for each device as it\'92s connected and then give the option to export the entire session as one file. If this is not possible, the description should be updated to guide the users exactly what should be done. \
\
Currently this only reads compatible devices. On first try from macbook on Brave browser (that\'92s built on Chrome), it didnt read the old Samsung Non Android device, a USB stick and the Kobo Libra 2 reader. Even though, the Samsung and the Kobo were charging through the USB on the macbook and on the windows, I could browse the folder structure and copy paste files. So some connection existed. The tool just didn\'92t identify it. \
\
Ideally, the tool should handle any incompatible device with grace, now im not sure if this is due to limitation of what devices can be read through the web at all, or the limitation of the WebUSB tool that we built. If the macbook and windows are both able to connect the device in any form but the webusb is unable to read it due to technical limitation or whatever, it should be handled gracefully. \
\
On the windows machine, there were two ghost devices that it identified, but nothing physical was connected. So it was probably software driven since it was listed on every device i plugged in. Not sure what to make of this or how it affects what we\'92re doing. \
\
